# Skill section Strategies
## Combine skills: To remove clutter
If skills are not relevant to the job vacancy try to combine them
Example1: DHCP, DNS, LAN, WiFi can be combined into Networking if they are not relevant to the job vacancy
Example2: Python, Django, Docker can be combined into Python Development if they are not relevant to the job vacancy
Example3: LLM, RAG, GPT, Git, Langchain, Langgraph, Langsmith, Ragas can be combined into LLM Development if they are not relevant to the job vacancy
## Combine skills: To be more relevant
Try to make unimportant skills to the job vacancy more relevant by combining them
Example1: For a job about docker, DNS, DHCP, LAN, WIFI can be combined into Networking, as Networking is a part of docker, so it removes clutter and makes the skill more relevant to the job vacancy
Example2: For a job vacancy about system engineering where they value powershell automation in the job vacancy you can combine Django, Python, Flask into something that is closer to powershell and automation like "Python Scripting and Automation"
## Keep detailed summing of skills if they are relevant to the job
Example1: If the job vacancy is about system engineering where they state DHCP an DNS, than you should keep the skills DHCP, DNS, LAN, WIFI separate as they are relevant to the job vacancy.
## Renaming skills to match the job vacancy
Example1: "Powershell" can be changed to "PowerShell Programming" in a job where python is important, because powershell programming is closer to python than just powershell as it emphasizes the programming aspect of powershell)
Example2: If the job vacancy talks about GCP, and the CV has Google Cloud, than rename the skill to GCP to match the job vacancy
Example3: If communication is important in the job vacancy, than rename "Sales", "Customer Service" to "Communicating with Customers (Sales, Customer Service)"
## Combine strategies above:
You can combine strategies above to remove clutter and make skills more relevant to the job vacancy
## Remove skills:
All the rules above should be preferred, it is better to group or rename skills than to remove them,
but if a skill are not relevant at all and not group or rename than you can remove them. Make sure that each experience has at least 1 skill left, choose the most relevant skill to keep if you have to remove skills.
## Important:
Maintain overview of the larger picture, all these examples where about isolated skills, but you should always look
at the larger picture and see if the skills are relevant in the context of the job vacancy.

